# The Old Chisholm Trail: traditional cowboy song, text after Lomax, Cowboy Songs (1910).
{title: The Old Chisholm Trail}
{composer: Traditional (USA, cowboy)}
{key: G}
{tempo: 120}
{time: 4/4}
{x_level: 1}
{x_strum: D - D - D - D -}

{comment: Quarter-note downs to start; later try D - D U - U D U.}

{start_of_grid label="Verse"}
| G . . . |
| G . . . |
| D . . . |
| G . . . |
{end_of_grid}

{start_of_grid label="Chorus"}
| G . . . | C . . . |
| D . . . | G . . . |
{end_of_grid}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
Oh, [G]come along, boys,
And listen to my tale,
I'll [D]tell you all my troubles
On the [G]old Chisholm trail.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Coma ti yi youpy, [C]youpy ya, youpy ya,
[D]Coma ti yi youpy, [G]youpy ya.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
I [G]started up the trail
October twenty-third,
I [D]started up the trail
With the [G]2-U herd.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
I [G]woke up one morning
On the old Chisholm trail,
[D]Rope in my hand
And a [G]cow by the tail.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
